{"id":"sagemaker-unified-studio","corpus":"aws","title":"Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio","sourceUrl":"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/sagemaker-unified-studio/latest/userguide/what-is-sagemaker-unified-studio.html","license":"AWS Documentation © Amazon Web Services, Inc.","blocks":[{"kind":"h1","text":"Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio"},{"kind":"p","text":"As a part of the next generation of Amazon SageMaker, the Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio is a unified development experience that brings together AWS data, analytics, artificial intelligence (AI), and machine learning (ML) services. It provides a place to build, deploy, execute, and monitor workflows from a single interface. This helps drive collaboration across teams and facilitate agile development."},{"kind":"p","text":"In Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio, administrators manage the users and groups that can access Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio, and they set up resources for teams to use. When your administrator grants you access to Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio, you can contribute to Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio projects. Within Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio projects, you can collaborate on business use cases by creating and sharing data, computation work, and other resources."},{"kind":"p","text":"This guide provides information about using Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio to create, contribute to, and manage projects. For more information about the administrator experience and flow for creating, configuring, and managing your domains, see the Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio Administrator Guide."},{"kind":"h2","text":"How does it work?"},{"kind":"p","text":"After your administrator has set up your domain and invited you to use Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio, you can start creating, managing, and using projects."},{"kind":"p","text":"The flow for Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio users is as follows:"},{"kind":"li","text":"Gain access to Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio by configuring your single sign-on (SSO) or IAM credentials and using the domain URL from your administrator."},{"kind":"li","text":"Create a new project or navigate to a project that you have been added to."},{"kind":"li","text":"Use the tools and resources within Amazon SageMaker Unified Studio to build, share, and execute applications within your project."}],"lemmas":{"amazons":["amazon","amazons"],"unified":["unified","unify"],"unifieds":["unifieds","unified"],"unifies":["unifies","unify"],"studios":["studio","studios"],"parts":["part","parts"],"parted":["parted","part"],"parting":["parting","part"],"nexts":["nexts","next"],"generations":["generation","generations"],"developments":["development","developments"],"experiences":["experience","experiences"],"experienced":["experienced","experience"],"experiencing":["experiencing","experience"],"brings":["brings","bring"],"bringing":["bringing","bring"],"brought":["brought","bring"],"togethers":["togethers","together"],"data":["datum","data"],"artificials":["artificials","artificial"],"intelligences":["intelligence","intelligences"],"machines":["machine","machines"],"machining":["machining","machine"],"learning":["learning","learn"],"learnings":["learning","learnings"],"learns":["learns","learn"],"learned":["learned","learn"],"services":["service","services"],"serviced":["serviced","service"],"servicing":["servicing","service"],"provides":["provides","provide"],"provided":["provided","provide"],"providing":["providing","provide"],"places":["place","places"],"placing":["placing","place"],"placed":["placed","place"],"builds":["build","builds"],"building":["building","build"],"built":["built","build"],"deploys":["deploys","deploy"],"deployed":["deployed","deploy"],"deploying":["deploying","deploy"],"executes":["executes","execute"],"executed":["executed","execute"],"executing":["executing","execute"],"monitors":["monitor","monitors"],"monitored":["monitored","monitor"],"monitoring":["monitoring","monitor"],"workflows":["workflow","workflows"],"singles":["sin